From 162fbd267e79c28012f1827b7757c996fe1f7050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:06:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 136/144] video: every video player shares the GPU's primary
 CUDA context

libmpv's CUDA hwdec interop creates a CUDA context in every render context, and FFmpeg one per copy decoder, so each
video texture of a scene paid for a context of its own: 160 MiB of device memory on an RTX 3070 Ti, a scene with two
1080p videos 320 MiB of it. Nothing needs them apart: the players run in one process on one GPU.

GLPlayer now asks libmpv for `cuda-primary-context` (an mpv option from a patch liascape carries, offered upstream):
the interop then retains the device's primary context instead of creating one and releases it when the player's render
context goes, so every player in the process shares that one context, decoding with nvdec on it as before. A libmpv
without the option refuses it and keeps a context per player, exactly as before; no host call is needed.

Measured with liascape's host_api_test (two 64 x 64 video textures, NVIDIA): the second video adds 0-1 MiB instead of
169 MiB; the primary context is released when the last player goes; a second scene's video keeps decoding when the
first scene and its two videos close.

Origin: ours
Why: liascape docs/TODO.md #104 (scene video texture VRAM)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/linux-wallpaperengine/context.h                 | 4 +++-
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux-wallpaperengine/context.h b/include/linux-wallpaperengine/context.h
index 1252323..2dd28d1 100644
--- a/include/linux-wallpaperengine/context.h
+++ b/include/linux-wallpaperengine/context.h
@@ -142,7 +142,9 @@ WPENGINE_API void wp_context_set_gl_upload_context (wp_context* context, wp_gl_u
  * host that knows its GPU names the one it decodes with (`cuda`, `vaapi`, ...) or `no` (copy modes only) and an `hwdec`
  * list that suits it. Set it before the first wp_render_frame;
  * a player already started keeps what it had. NULL leaves that value at libmpv's default (`hwdec` `auto`,
- * `gpu-hwdec-interop` `auto`)
+ * `gpu-hwdec-interop` `auto`). Whatever is set, every player also asks libmpv for `cuda-primary-context`, so with the
+ * CUDA interop or a CUDA decoder they all share the GPU's primary CUDA context instead of making one each (a libmpv
+ * without that option keeps one per player)
  *
  * @param context The context to set it for
  * @param hwdec libmpv's `hwdec` value (e.g. "nvdec,nvdec-copy,auto-copy"), or NULL
diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp
index f1b2dd6..f845a87 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/VideoPlayback/MPV/GLPlayer.cpp
@@ -324,6 +324,10 @@ void GLPlayer::init () {
 	mpv_set_option_string (this->m_handle, "gpu-hwdec-interop", context.video_hwdec_interop->c_str ());
     }
     mpv_set_option_string (this->m_handle, "hwdec", context.video_hwdec.value_or ("auto").c_str ());
+    // every player in the process decodes on the GPU's one primary CUDA context rather than making its own (each costs
+    // device memory: 160 MiB on an RTX 3070 Ti, so a scene with two videos paid twice). A libmpv without the option
+    // (the option comes from a patch to mpv) refuses it and keeps a context per player
+    mpv_set_option_string (this->m_handle, "cuda-primary-context", "yes");
 
     if (mpv_initialize (this->m_handle) < 0) {
 	sLog.exception ("Could not initialize mpv context");
